CORE
main.cpp
--cpp26
^file main\.cpp line \d+: static assertion failed: f\(\) is 4$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
static_assert condition is not a constant expression
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
The program is ill-formed: GCC 16 reports "static assertion failed: f() is
4".  CBMC's constant evaluator did not evaluate throw and try
(cpp26_constexpr_exception), and a static_assert whose condition it could
not evaluate was skipped with a warning, so verification succeeded; it must
not be reported as "not a constant expression" either.  The
static_assert is the check that must fail, so there is no WRONG assertion.
